* Constant On-Time Lab -- generic educational COT controller blocks
* Requires COT_ONESHOT.lib in the calling deck.

.MODEL D_CTRL_COTLAB D (IS=1n N=1 RS=1m TT=1n CJO=1p)

* COT_REQUEST FB REF RIPPLE REQUEST
* REQUEST rises when REF > FB + RIPPLE. TDELAY is represented by a first-order
* lag, not an exact transport delay. VSOFT smooths the ideal comparison.
* VHYST applies bounded positive feedback through the delayed REQUEST state;
* it is an educational hysteresis approximation rather than device physics.
.SUBCKT COT_REQUEST FB REF RIPPLE REQUEST PARAMS:
+ VLOGIC=1 VSOFT=1m VHYST=0 TDELAY=10n CDELAY=10p
ECOMP CRAW 0 VALUE={LIMIT(0.5*VLOGIC*(1+
+ TANH((V(REF)-V(FB)-V(RIPPLE)+
+ VHYST*(V(REQUEST)/VLOGIC-0.5))/VSOFT)),0,VLOGIC)}
RDELAY CRAW CDELAYN {IF(TDELAY>0,TDELAY/(0.693*CDELAY),1m)}
CDELAYX CDELAYN 0 {CDELAY} IC=0
EREQ REQUEST 0 VALUE={IF(V(CDELAYN)>VLOGIC/2,VLOGIC,0)}
RREQ REQUEST 0 1G
.ENDS COT_REQUEST

* COT_CURRENT_LIMIT ISENSE ILIMITNODE TRIP
* ISENSE is 1 V/A by convention. ILIMITNODE permits a dynamic threshold.
.SUBCKT COT_CURRENT_LIMIT ISENSE ILIMITNODE TRIP PARAMS:
+ VLOGIC=1 VSOFT=2m TDELAY=5n CDELAY=10p
ETRIPRAW TRIPRAW 0 VALUE={LIMIT(0.5*VLOGIC*(1+
+ TANH((V(ISENSE)-V(ILIMITNODE))/VSOFT)),0,VLOGIC)}
RILIMDELAY TRIPRAW TRIPD {IF(TDELAY>0,TDELAY/(0.693*CDELAY),1m)}
CILIMDELAY TRIPD 0 {CDELAY} IC=0
ETRIP TRIP 0 VALUE={IF(V(TRIPD)>VLOGIC/2,VLOGIC,0)}
RTRIP TRIP 0 1G
.ENDS COT_CURRENT_LIMIT

* Fixed-on-time composite controller.
* COT_CONTROLLER FB REF RIPPLE ISENSE GATE REQUEST READY
.SUBCKT COT_CONTROLLER FB REF RIPPLE ISENSE GATE REQUEST READY PARAMS:
+ TON=800n TONMIN=100n TONMAX=2u TOFFMIN=100n ILIMIT=20
+ VLOGIC=1 VSOFT=1m VHYST=0 TDELAY=10n ILIMDELAY=5n
VILIMIT ILIM 0 {ILIMIT}
XREQ FB REF RIPPLE REQUEST COT_REQUEST PARAMS:
+ VLOGIC={VLOGIC} VSOFT={VSOFT} VHYST={VHYST} TDELAY={TDELAY}
XCL ISENSE ILIM TRIP COT_CURRENT_LIMIT PARAMS:
+ VLOGIC={VLOGIC} TDELAY={ILIMDELAY}
XSHOT REQUEST TRIP GATE READY COT_ONESHOT PARAMS:
+ TON={LIMIT(TON,TONMIN,TONMAX)} TOFFMIN={TOFFMIN} VLOGIC={VLOGIC}
.ENDS COT_CONTROLLER

* Adaptive-on-time composite. TPERIOD is a timing-law constant:
* TON = clamp(TPERIOD*VREF/VIN, TONMIN, TONMAX).
* This is one representative feed-forward law, not a universal architecture.
* COT_ADAPTIVE_CONTROLLER VIN FB REF RIPPLE ISENSE
*                         GATE REQUEST READY TONMON
.SUBCKT COT_ADAPTIVE_CONTROLLER VIN FB REF RIPPLE ISENSE
+ GATE REQUEST READY TONMON PARAMS:
+ TPERIOD=2u TONMIN=100n TONMAX=2u TOFFMIN=100n ILIMIT=20
+ VINMIN=1 VLOGIC=1 VSOFT=1m VHYST=0 TDELAY=10n ILIMDELAY=5n
VILIMIT ILIM 0 {ILIMIT}
ETON TONMON 0 VALUE={LIMIT(TPERIOD*V(REF)/
+ IF(V(VIN)>VINMIN,V(VIN),VINMIN),TONMIN,TONMAX)}
XREQ FB REF RIPPLE REQUEST COT_REQUEST PARAMS:
+ VLOGIC={VLOGIC} VSOFT={VSOFT} VHYST={VHYST} TDELAY={TDELAY}
XCL ISENSE ILIM TRIP COT_CURRENT_LIMIT PARAMS:
+ VLOGIC={VLOGIC} TDELAY={ILIMDELAY}
XSHOT REQUEST TRIP TONMON GATE READY COT_ONESHOT_CMD PARAMS:
+ TONMIN={TONMIN} TONMAX={TONMAX} TOFFMIN={TOFFMIN} VLOGIC={VLOGIC}
.ENDS COT_ADAPTIVE_CONTROLLER

* Optional slow DC servo. Its output is intended to trim REF or FB while the
* ripple comparator continues to set pulse timing.
* COT_DC_SERVO FB REF TRIM
.SUBCKT COT_DC_SERVO FB REF TRIM PARAMS:
+ GM=50u CCOMP=100n RLEAK=1MEG TRIMMAX=100m
GERR 0 NCOMP VALUE={GM*(V(REF)-V(FB))}
CCOMP NCOMP 0 {CCOMP} IC=0
RLEAK NCOMP 0 {RLEAK}
ETRIM TRIM 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(NCOMP),-TRIMMAX,TRIMMAX)}
RTRIM TRIM 0 1G
.ENDS COT_DC_SERVO
